        "root_concepts": "[digital, disruption]",
        "section": "papermaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Digital Disruption and the Paper Industry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   OFFICE PAPER DEMAND (US, million short tons):\n   ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n   1990:   ~5 Mt/yr   (pre-internet, photocopiers everywhere)\n   2000:   ~8 Mt/yr   (peak U.S. office paper — internet coexisting)\n   2007:   ~7.5 Mt/yr (global peak for P&W)\n   2019:   ~5 Mt/yr   (pre-COVID)\n   2022:   ~3.5 Mt/yr (accelerated by remote work)\n   2023:   ~3.2 Mt/yr (continuing decline ~6%/yr)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:papermaking:08-digital-disruption, git-history:papermaking:08-digital-disruption]",
        "canonical_path": "papermaking/08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md",
        "concepts": "[digital, disruption]",
        "current_path": "papermaking/08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:papermaking:digital-disruption",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "papermaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[digital, disruption]",
        "section": "papermaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Digital Disruption and the Paper Industry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The \"paperless office\" predicted in 1975 didn't happen until ~2010–2020 as\ndigital workflow matured. Three enabling technology waves:"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md#009",
      "path": [
        "08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:papermaking:08-digital-disruption, git-history:papermaking:08-digital-disruption]",
        "canonical_path": "papermaking/08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md",
        "concepts": "[digital, disruption]",
        "current_path": "papermaking/08-DIGITAL-DISRUPTION.md",
        "id": "maxim:papermaking:digital-disruption",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "papermaking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[digital, disruption]",
        "section": "papermaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Digital Disruption and the Paper Industry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   WAVE 1 (1990s): Email → reduces correspondence paper\n   WAVE 2 (2000s): PDF + laser printer → reduces document distribution\n                    but INCREASES printing for personal use temporarily\n   WAVE 3 (2010s): Tablet + smartphone + cloud storage → digital-native\n                    workflows, electronic signatures, EHR in medical\n                    → terminal decline in office paper\n   WAVE 4 (2020–): COVID remote work → permanent change in office paper demand\n                    Return to office (partial) → demand plateau at lower level\n```"
    },
    {
